{"result":{"status":200,"page":"y0ssq","data":{"userDefinedFilter":{},"items":[{"introduction":"Foraging for wild foods, particularly fungi or mushrooms, has been a great experience for both me and my husband. We have a good friend who is a retired forester from the Bureau of Land Management where we live in Southern Oregon. When he started showing us about the mushrooms that he knew were edible, we were hooked. He showed us that there are many fungi that are easily identifiable and plentiful in the areas where we regularly hunt for deer and we discovered an entirely new way to fill our freezer and pantry!","servings":"variable","photo":"wix:image://v1/577c92_27fb2a79fb6746df8c1071d99febd701~mv2.jpg/Lyophyllum%20decastes,%20Fried%20Chicken%20Mushrooms.jpg#originWidth=4032&originHeight=3024","url":"https://www.theglasspantry.com/harvesting-and-preserving-wild-mushrooms","link-recipes-1-1-title":"/mushrooms1/harvesting-and-preserving-wild-mushrooms","_id":"56e11185-f3b1-4831-b4dc-3856fba2e714","_owner":"577c92d8-55f7-4f98-88a2-d8647b1c2c9c","_createdDate":{"$date":"2023-03-08T18:37:48.311Z"},"shortDescription":"Learn easy methods for cleaning, preserving and cooking a variety of commonly foraged wild mushrooms of the Pacific Northwest.","cookingTime":"Variable","_updatedDate":{"$date":"2023-03-08T23:37:06.794Z"},"preparationTime":"Variable","order":1.0,"ingredients":{"nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"foo","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Learn easy methods for cleaning, preserving and cooking a variety of commonly foraged wild mushrooms of the Pacific Northwest.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"","foreground":"rgb(28, 28, 28)"}}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0.0}}],"metadata":{"version":1.0,"createdTimestamp":"2023-03-08T23:37:04.765Z","updatedTimestamp":"2023-03-08T23:37:04.765Z","id":"dd67bb03-828a-41d9-9604-b59558ab31ea"},"documentStyle":{}},"catagory":"Wild Mushrooms","title":"Harvesting and Preserving Wild Mushrooms","link-recipes-1-1-all":"/wild-mushrooms/"},{"introduction":"This is where I will tell you all about my personal experiences harvesting, cleaning, freezing, dehydrating and cooking wild Morels. I hesitate to call them mushrooms as they are not truly mushrooms but they are a prized and delicious fungi that holds a very special place in our kitchen.","servings":"variable","photo":"wix:image://v1/577c92_29ee99dfc97744c9a046ef39afa47dd0~mv2.jpg/20220609_170856.jpg#originWidth=4032&originHeight=3024","url":"https://www.theglasspantry.com/morel-morchella-info","link-recipes-1-1-title":"/mushrooms1/morel---morchella","_id":"b5338150-9c9f-4d5f-a262-75c3d4a091e0","_owner":"577c92d8-55f7-4f98-88a2-d8647b1c2c9c","_createdDate":{"$date":"2023-03-08T18:37:48.312Z"},"shortDescription":"This is where I will tell you all about my personal experiences harvesting, cleaning, freezing, dehydrating and cooking wild Morels. I hesitate to call them mushrooms as they are not truly mushrooms but they are a prized and delicious fungi that holds a very special place in our kitchen.","cookingTime":"Variable","_updatedDate":{"$date":"2023-03-08T23:27:41.422Z"},"preparationTime":"Quick to clean and prep","order":2.0,"ingredients":{"nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"foo","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"When you are ready to prepare them, simply cut them in half and let them soak for a few minutes then give them a quick brush with a soft bristled toothbrush if they still have anything left in the crevice's. Set them out to dry until you are ready to finish preparing them.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":"rgb(28, 28, 28)"}}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0.0}}],"metadata":{"version":1.0,"createdTimestamp":"2023-03-08T23:14:56.354Z","updatedTimestamp":"2023-03-08T23:14:56.354Z","id":"c600ba7f-424c-4ea0-a114-783e7fe898c8"},"documentStyle":{}},"catagory":"Wild Mushrooms","title":"Morel - Morchella","link-recipes-1-1-all":"/wild-mushrooms/"},{"introduction":"Candied Witches Butter is a sweet treat that resembles sour gummy candy and has wonderful good things inside to help keep you healthy. I'm not a nutritionist so please look up the properties of Tremella mesenterica and Tremella aurentia, commonly known as Witches Butter, to see what I mean. Witches Butter is a very easily identified fungus you can find in nearly any forest.","servings":"variable","photo":"wix:image://v1/577c92_085ed5afbb754eedbd8061f534d40795~mv2.jpg/20211202_160844.jpg#originWidth=4032&originHeight=3024","url":"http://www.theglasspantry.com/candied-witches-butter","link-recipes-1-1-title":"/mushrooms1/candied-witches-butter-","_id":"e01b36e8-b85c-4352-a7c1-f1d78a74b3a8","_owner":"577c92d8-55f7-4f98-88a2-d8647b1c2c9c","_createdDate":{"$date":"2023-03-08T18:37:48.313Z"},"shortDescription":"Candied Witches Butter is a sweet treat that resembles sour gummy candy and has wonderful good things inside to help keep you healthy. I'm not a nutritionist so please look up the properties of Tremella mesenterica and Tremella aurentia, commonly known as Witches Butter, to see what I mean. Witches Butter is a very easily identified fungus you can find in nearly any forest.","cookingTime":"15 minutes + dehydrating and aging","_updatedDate":{"$date":"2023-03-08T23:28:13.135Z"},"recipesCatagoryCatagory":"/Recipes/catagory/Wild-Mushrooms","preparationTime":"30 hands on time","order":3.0,"ingredients":{"nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"foo","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"1/3 - 1/2 cup Witches Butter Pieces","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0.0}},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"qxkhq2555","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"1/2 cup simple syrup - ( or boil equal parts granulated sugar and water to make 1/2 cup simple syrup)","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"cnucv2557","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"1/4 teaspoon lemon extract","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"c8hbd2559","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"1/4 teaspoon citric acid","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"gxon82561","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"2-3 tablespoons granulated sugar divided, more if needed","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"}],"metadata":{"version":1.0,"createdTimestamp":"2023-03-08T19:21:42.626Z","updatedTimestamp":"2023-03-08T19:21:42.626Z","id":"a2593b25-2c93-47e1-be3a-29b0ff4cf327"},"documentStyle":{}},"catagory":"Wild Mushrooms","steps":{"nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"foo","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Rinse the witches butter thoroughly to remove debris.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0.0}},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"l4ohu2431","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"​","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"9rw7z2433","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Heat simple syrup, lemon extract and citric acid to a low boil.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"wo8lf2435","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"​","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"s7b6p2437","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Add the witches butter and reduce heat. Simmer for 15 minutes or so then remove the pan from heat and allow the contents to cool for 15 minutes or more.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"gqh5e2439","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"​","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"o140z2441","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Dehydrate","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}},{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700.0},{"type":"ITALIC"}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"bbnxt2443","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"​","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"7wx982445","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Remove the witches butter from the liquid and chop the witches butter into smaller pieces if necessary to get evenly sized pieces.","decorations":[]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"y92bw2447","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"​","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"x4lc92449","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Place the pieces on parchment paper and dehydrate on a vegetable setting or at 135 degrees for 4-5 hours or as needed to reduce the liquid until the witches butter is sticky and gummy. ","decorations":[]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"m42gi2451","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"​","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"1w6b72453","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Allow it to cool to room temperature, then use a sharp knife to peel the witches butter pieces off of the parchment and place the pieces one at a time into a small glass jar with a tablespoon of sugar, swirling to coat the gummies to keep them from sticking together. Add another tablespoon or about half way through until all of the witches butter pieces are in the jar and evenly coated with sugar. Add a little more citric acid if you like your gummies more sour.","decorations":[]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"tx2eb2455","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"​","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"j60j52457","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Close the jar tightly and shake daily, adding sugar and or citric acid as necessary, aging the witches butter for 3 weeks or until the gummies have plumped to your liking.","decorations":[]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"}],"metadata":{"version":1.0,"createdTimestamp":"2023-03-08T19:21:42.706Z","updatedTimestamp":"2023-03-08T19:21:42.706Z","id":"d6500a3d-04b4-40c6-8baa-d663be6d58c5"},"documentStyle":{}},"instructions":"Rinse the witches butter thoroughly to remove debris.\n\n​\n\nHeat simple syrup, lemon extract and citric acid to a low boil.\n\n​\n\nAdd the witches butter and reduce heat. Simmer for 15 minutes or so then remove the pan from heat and allow the contents to cool for 15 minutes or more.\n\n​\n\nDehydrate\n\n​\n\nRemove the witches butter from the liquid and chop the witches butter into smaller pieces if necessary to get evenly sized pieces.\n\n​\n\nPlace the pieces on parchment paper and dehydrate on a vegetable setting or at 135 degrees for 4-5 hours or as needed to reduce the liquid until the witches butter is sticky and gummy. \n\n​\n\nAllow it to cool to room temperature, then use a sharp knife to peel the witches butter pieces off of the parchment and place the pieces one at a time into a small glass jar with a tablespoon of sugar, swirling to coat the gummies to keep them from sticking together. Add another tablespoon or about half way through until all of the witches butter pieces are in the jar and evenly coated with sugar. Add a little more citric acid if you like your gummies more sour.\n\n​\n\nClose the jar tightly and shake daily, adding sugar and or citric acid as necessary, aging the witches butter for 3 weeks or until the gummies have plumped to your liking.","title":"Candied Witches Butter ","link-recipes-1-1-all":"/wild-mushrooms/"},{"introduction":"These are my personal experiences harvesting, cleaning, freezing, dehydrating and cooking wild oyster mushrooms. These mushrooms are prolific in the Pacific Northwest and they can be found any time conditions are right for them all year long. Delicious and fairly easy to identify, there are many varieties including a late harvest oyster I'm particularly fond of.","servings":"variable","photo":"wix:image://v1/577c92_8a909a94ade349939e7c7346f7c2bd8f~mv2.jpg/20211019_165000.jpg#originWidth=4032&originHeight=3024","url":"https://www.theglasspantry.com/pleurotus-oystermushrooms","link-recipes-1-1-title":"/mushrooms1/pleurotus---oyster-mushrooms","_id":"8d608376-5181-410b-bf92-cd8efdaf02c2","_owner":"577c92d8-55f7-4f98-88a2-d8647b1c2c9c","_createdDate":{"$date":"2023-03-19T22:10:00.900Z"},"shortDescription":"These are my personal experiences harvesting, cleaning, freezing, dehydrating and cooking wild oyster mushrooms. These mushrooms are prolific in the Pacific Northwest and they can be found any time conditions are right for them all year long. Delicious and fairly easy to identify, there are many varieties including a late harvest oyster I'm particularly fond of.","cookingTime":"Variable","_updatedDate":{"$date":"2023-03-23T21:48:27.611Z"},"preparationTime":"Variable","order":4.0,"ingredients":{"nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"foo","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Oysters are easy to clean. Do not clean them with anything but a dry brush or towel until you are ready to cook or otherwise preserve them.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"","foreground":"rgb(28, 28, 28)"}}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0.0}}],"metadata":{"version":1.0,"createdTimestamp":"2023-03-19T22:16:15.479Z","updatedTimestamp":"2023-03-19T22:16:15.479Z","id":"672b61c4-e81f-46f6-8ea1-63b260b1114e"},"documentStyle":{}},"catagory":"Wild Mushrooms","instructions":"Oysters are easy to clean. Do not clean them with anything but a dry brush or towel until you are ready to cook or otherwise preserve them.","title":"Pleurotus - Oyster Mushrooms","link-recipes-1-1-all":"/wild-mushrooms/"},{"introduction":"Have you ever wanted to grow gourmet mushrooms at home? You can! Many people like me have found growing their own mushrooms to be a truly rewarding experience and those that haven't probably just need a few tips to make it happen. ","servings":"variable","photo":"wix:image://v1/577c92_559c4d1cb3ec40eaa778d1b4e0a75056~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg/20190809_091740.jpg#originWidth=4032&originHeight=3024","url":"https://www.theglasspantry.com/grow-blue-oyster-mushrooms","link-recipes-1-1-title":"/mushrooms1/growing-blue-oyster-mushrooms-at-home","_id":"212de743-284e-40ed-b92f-b20d5e87e3be","_owner":"577c92d8-55f7-4f98-88a2-d8647b1c2c9c","_createdDate":{"$date":"2023-03-08T18:41:36.543Z"},"shortDescription":"Have you ever wanted to grow gourmet mushrooms at home? You can! Many people like me have found growing their own mushrooms to be a truly rewarding experience and those that haven't probably just need a few tips to make it happen. ","cookingTime":"Quick","_updatedDate":{"$date":"2023-03-19T22:14:10.269Z"},"preparationTime":"Quick to clean and prep","order":5.0,"ingredients":{"nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"foo","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"You need to have a space about 18\" square where your mushrooms will receive at least 6 hours of good indirect light. Mine do get a short amount of direct light but it's never too strong or for more than a few hours. It's a myth that mushrooms want a super cool dark place.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"","foreground":"rgb(28, 28, 28)"}}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0.0}}],"metadata":{"version":1.0,"createdTimestamp":"2023-03-08T23:16:26.241Z","updatedTimestamp":"2023-03-08T23:16:26.241Z","id":"c60b40dc-773b-405a-9596-ab746d049d21"},"documentStyle":{}},"catagory":"Wild Mushrooms","title":"Growing Blue Oyster Mushrooms at Home","link-recipes-1-1-all":"/wild-mushrooms/"},{"introduction":"These are my personal experiences harvesting, cleaning, freezing, dehydrating and cooking Coral Mushrooms - Ramaria. Coral mushrooms are prolific in the Pacific Northwest and they can be found any time conditions are right for them all year long. Delicious and easy to identify, there are many color variations around the world, we typically find yellow and pink ones. I think I prefer the yellow.","servings":"variable","photo":"wix:image://v1/577c92_26d41a12b33b4fe98da68a10dcae929d~mv2.jpg/20230321_115914.jpg#originWidth=3024&originHeight=4032","url":"https://www.theglasspantry.com/coralmushrooms-ramaria","link-recipes-1-1-title":"/mushrooms1/coral-mushrooms---ramaria","_id":"28e3b4c3-db15-4bac-830d-5c998f570c56","_owner":"577c92d8-55f7-4f98-88a2-d8647b1c2c9c","_createdDate":{"$date":"2023-03-23T21:34:59.081Z"},"shortDescription":"These are my personal experiences harvesting, cleaning, freezing, dehydrating and cooking Coral Mushrooms - Ramaria. Coral mushrooms are prolific in the Pacific Northwest and they can be found any time conditions are right for them all year long. Delicious and easy to identify, there are many color variations around the world, we typically find yellow and pink ones. I think I prefer the yellow.","cookingTime":"Variable","_updatedDate":{"$date":"2023-03-23T22:02:48.197Z"},"preparationTime":"Variable","order":6.0,"ingredients":{"nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"foo","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"When you are ready to prepare them, start by pulling them apart into smaller pieces so you can work them with a soft bristle toothbrush using tapping motions to remove pine needles and debris","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"","foreground":"rgb(28, 28, 28)"}}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0.0}}],"metadata":{"version":1.0,"createdTimestamp":"2023-03-23T22:02:50.978Z","updatedTimestamp":"2023-03-23T22:02:50.978Z","id":"6da54eb6-86be-44f8-8053-fae6048c8093"},"documentStyle":{}},"catagory":"Wild Mushrooms","title":"Coral Mushrooms - Ramaria","link-recipes-1-1-all":"/wild-mushrooms/"},{"introduction":"This is a tasty dish my husband taught me! Well, he was making something similar for himself before we got married. His version was the basics, large Portobello mushrooms stuffed with mild Italian sausage then topped with mozzarella cheese. All baked together in yummy harmony. Really I just stepped it up with the addition of some mushroom marinara. Try this either way depending on how much time you have or how much energy you would like to put into dinner. Trust me it will be delicious!  ","servings":"4","photo":"image://v1/577c92_e1589c34a2774eb0ae6692de163e92c3~mv2.jpg/1500_1125/20171230_185429_edited.jpg","url":"http://www.theglasspantry.com/single-post/2018/03/10/Sausage-Stuffed-Portabello-Mushrooms","link-recipes-1-1-title":"/mushrooms1/sausage-stuffed-portabello-mushrooms-","_id":"2230fb37-bc26-4a7c-b65d-7403188b77e1","_owner":"577c92d8-55f7-4f98-88a2-d8647b1c2c9c","_createdDate":{"$date":"2023-03-08T18:37:48.308Z"},"shortDescription":"This is a tasty dish my husband taught me! Well, he was making something similar for himself before we got married. His version was the basics, large Portobello mushrooms stuffed with mild Italian sausage then topped with mozzarella cheese. All baked together in yummy harmony. Really I just stepped it up with the addition of some mushroom marinara. Try this either way depending on how much time you have or how much energy you would like to put into dinner. Trust me it will be delicious!  ","cookingTime":"50-60 minutes","_updatedDate":{"$date":"2023-03-08T20:24:46.327Z"},"recipesCatagoryCatagory":"/Recipes/catagory/Wild-Mushrooms","preparationTime":"30 minutes","order":7.0,"ingredients":{"nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"foo","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"For the mushrooms","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":