"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Remove the large stem from the mushrooms and chop them up to add to the sauce. Make 4 balls of mild Italian sausage, place one into each mushroom cap and flatten it out like a hamburger. Place the stuffed mushrooms in a shallow baking dish with enough water to cover the bottom of the dish 1/4 inch deep then into the oven preheated to 350 degrees.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"var(--ricos-custom-p-background-color,unset)","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"orfe15335","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"viewer-o8np","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"pn2gf5336","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"viewer-5n5ta","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Make the Marinara","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"var(--ricos-custom-p-background-color,unset)","foreground":""}},{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700.0}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"ozcs05338","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"viewer-rgf6","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Add the onions to a sauce pan with a tablespoon of olive oil and saute' them until they are translucent. Now add the garlic for just a minute or two then stir in the rest of the ingredients. I add the chopped mushrooms last so they wouldn't cook down too much and still retain some of their texture. Bring the pot to a low boil then reduce the heat to low and let it simmer for twenty minutes or so. Add the truffle or mushroom oil now if using.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"var(--ricos-custom-p-background-color,unset)","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"mxdu65340","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"viewer-1vg6i","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"yxvug5341","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"viewer-217k4","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Top and finish the mushrooms","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"var(--ricos-custom-p-background-color,unset)","foreground":""}},{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700.0}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"stm2t5343","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"viewer-f10i1","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"With a meat thermometer, check to be sure the sausage in the mushrooms is cooked to 160 degrees before adding a dollop of marinara sauce and nice handful of grated mozzarella cheese. Preheat the broiler on the oven then put the topped mushrooms back into the oven to brown the tops. Watch closely. They should be nicely browned in 4-5 minutes.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"var(--ricos-custom-p-background-color,unset)","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"}],"metadata":{"version":1.0,"createdTimestamp":"2023-03-08T19:32:32.369Z","updatedTimestamp":"2023-03-08T19:32:32.369Z","id":"41cba47f-2e81-4d61-bffd-4ddf7aef8892"},"documentStyle":{}},"instructions":"Start the mushrooms\n\nRemove the large stem from the mushrooms and chop them up to add to the sauce. Make 4 balls of mild Italian sausage, place one into each mushroom cap and flatten it out like a hamburger. Place the stuffed mushrooms in a shallow baking dish with enough water to cover the bottom of the dish 1/4 inch deep then into the oven preheated to 350 degrees.\n\n \n\nMake the Marinara\n\nAdd the onions to a sauce pan with a tablespoon of olive oil and saute' them until they are translucent. Now add the garlic for just a minute or two then stir in the rest of the ingredients. I add the chopped mushrooms last so they wouldn't cook down too much and still retain some of their texture. Bring the pot to a low boil then reduce the heat to low and let it simmer for twenty minutes or so. Add the truffle or mushroom oil now if using.\n\n \n\nTop and finish the mushrooms\n\nWith a meat thermometer, check to be sure the sausage in the mushrooms is cooked to 160 degrees before adding a dollop of marinara sauce and nice handful of grated mozzarella cheese. Preheat the broiler on the oven then put the topped mushrooms back into the oven to brown the tops. Watch closely. They should be nicely browned in 4-5 minutes.\n\n ","title":"Sausage Stuffed Portabello Mushrooms ","link-recipes-1-1-all":"/wild-mushrooms/"},{"introduction":"This is an incredibly yummy warm spring salad. It's really a stir-fry that I serve over salad instead of rice. It starts off with lot's of garlic because we all need more garlic. Then I toss in the veggies, the shrimp, some seasonings and some butter, stir-frying them quickly and gently because these are all tender things and it doesn't take much to overcook them.","servings":"2","photo":"image://v1/577c92_acc218f2a77c4a7299e6013602944a35~mv2.jpg/1500_1125/20180316_173930_edited.jpg","url":"https://www.theglasspantry.com/asparagus-shrimp-and-mushroom-skill","link-recipes-1-1-title":"/mushrooms1/asparagus%2C-shrimp-%26--mushroom-skillet-salad-","_id":"1762cc5f-1cdd-4bf6-bd92-cfac772e493e","_owner":"577c92d8-55f7-4f98-88a2-d8647b1c2c9c","_createdDate":{"$date":"2023-03-08T18:37:48.309Z"},"shortDescription":"This is an incredibly yummy warm spring salad. It's really a stir-fry that I se