agraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"whgcr1294","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Assemble the Casserole","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"pjkqw1296","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"​","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"k4l7j1298","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Preheat oven to 375 degrees.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"57ebe1300","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"​","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"fdiat1302","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Lightly spay oil a casserole then spread a thin layer of mushroom sauce on the bottom. Thinly layer potatoes, chicken filling, mushroom sauce and parsnips in that order 2 times then top with the mozzarella cheese.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"x8a4w1304","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"​","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"pbdc11306","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Bake at 375 degrees 45 - 60 minutes or until golden and bubbly.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"h57q81308","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Top with fresh chopped parsley and serve.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}}}],"metadata":{"version":1.0,"createdTimestamp":"2023-03-08T19:16:38.174Z","updatedTimestamp":"2023-03-08T19:16:38.174Z","id":"544c32c4-dbe1-4c3f-9ebd-730673fe319c"},"documentStyle":{}},"instructions":"Make the Mushroom sauce\n\n​\n\nHeat a small sauce pot on medium heat. Add the butter and flour and cook together until bubbly to make a light roux. Add the sliced mushrooms, minced garlic and minced onion mixing them together with the roux. \n\n​\n\nI have used store bought cremini in this recipe but Chanterelles, Fried Chicken mushrooms (Lyophyllum decastes), Honey Mushrooms (Armillaria), a variety of milk caps ( Lactarius), Oyster mushrooms or Shrimp Russula (Russula xerampelina) mushrooms would be very tasty in this dish.\n\n \n\n Important Note * If using wild mushrooms for this recipe, be sure you have properly identified the mushrooms and thoroughly cleaned and cooked them before adding them to this casserole. I like to use wild mushrooms that I have already prepared, sautéed and frozen, thaw just enough to loosen them and mix them in.\n\n​\n\nAdd the skim milk, stirring constantly until it comes to a boil and begins to thicken. Remove the pot from the heat and slowly stir in the whipping cream then season with nutmeg, salt and pepper.\n\n \n\nMake the Chicken filling\n\n​\n\nHeat a skillet on medium high heat. Add cooking oil, garlic, onion and chicken. Stir-fry until the vegetables are translucent and the chicken no longer pink. Add mushroom sauce to coat, then set aside.\n\n\nAssemble the Casserole\n\n​\n\nPreheat oven to 375 degrees.\n\n​\n\nLightly spay oil a casserole then spread a thin layer of mushroom sauce on the bottom. Thinly layer potatoes, chicken filling, mushroom sauce and parsnips in that order 2 times then top with the mozzarella cheese.\n\n​\n\nBake at 375 degrees 45 - 60 minutes or until golden and bubbly.\n\nTop with fresh chopped parsley and serve.","title":"Parsnip Potato Bake with Creamy Mushroom Sauce and Chicken ","link-recipes-1-1-all":"/wild-mushrooms/"},{"introduction":"I have used store bought cremini in this recipe but Fried Chicken mushrooms (Lyophyllum decastes), Honey Mushrooms (Armillaria), a variety of milk caps ( Lactarius), or Shrimp Russula (Russula xerampelina) mushrooms would be very tasty in this dish.","servings":"2","photo":"wix:image://v1/577c92_952b40dba4fb4c268cbacd2e0023e4bb~mv2.jpg/20200507_185942.jpg#originWidth=3352&originHeight=2514","url":"https://www.theglasspantry.com/escargot-stuffed-mushrooms","link-recipes-1-1-title":"/mushrooms1/escargot-stuffed-mushrooms","_id":"e81c28e0-4f88-4f7e-8c9c-93ae11ccdc8b","_owner":"577c92d8-55f7-4f98-88a2-d8647b1c2c9c","_createdDate":{"$date":"2023-03-08T18:37:48.315Z"},"shortDescription":"Harvesting your own snails requires some patience and a little bit of planning but on a daily basis you really do very little. You also control the exact day you would like to serve this divine little dish. It is also so much less traumatic than I first thought it would be. In fact it's quite simple and fascinating! I read through several recipes and articles describing the cleaning and preparing of snails until I came up with this method which works wonderfully for me.","cookingTime":"15 minutes but see note in ingredient list if using wild mushrooms.","_updatedDate":{"$date":"2023-03-08T20:24:58.962Z"},"recipesCatagoryCatagory":"/Recipes/catagory/Wild-Mushrooms","preparationTime":"45 minutes","order":11.0,"ingredients":{"nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"foo","nodes":[],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0.0}},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"comp-ka492x0n","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"9 - 12 ","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}},{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700.0}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"fresh garden snails","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}},{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700.0}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" that have been prepared for cooking by feeding them carrots or corn meal for 4-5 days then fasted for 5 days and washed thoroughly in cool clean water as described above.​2 tablespoons salt dissolved in 1 1/2 cups water.​1/4 cup white vinegar diluted with 3/4 cups water.​","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"12 evenly sized ","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}},{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700.0}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"i03sg968","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"gg0xi985","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"cremini mushrooms","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}},{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700.0}]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" cleaned and stemmed​I have used store bought cremini in this recipe but Fried Chicken mushrooms (Lyophyllum decastes), Honey Mushrooms (Armillaria), a variety of milk caps ( Lactarius), or Shrimp Russula (Russula xerampelina) mushrooms would be very tasty in this dish.","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":""}}]}}],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"8fopv1004","nodes":[],"type":"PARAGRAPH"},{"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"}},"style":{},"id":"4ensj1021","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[{"type":"COLOR","colorData":{"background":"transparent","foreground":